theorem a-row-multiplied-by-a-negative-number-read-from-its-other-side
  note        Multiplying 4·x − 5 ≤ 0 by −2 turns it round, to
              −8·x + 10 ≥ 0, which the row writes as 0 ≤ −8·x + 10: the same
              order read from its other side.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume 4·x − 5 ≤ 0                                                  (H2)
  then 0 ≤ −8·x + 10

1.  0 ≤ −8·x + 10
    inequalities
      4·x − 5 ≤ 0        H2
      0 ≤ −8·x + 10      multiplying by −2
